        "id": 1831528
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-07T08:50:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Isn\u0027t that case not possible because `slice` is already capped at `pos` characters long due to `slice \u003d \u0026line[..pos]`? So let\u0027s say `line` \u003d `\"hahahaha hihihi hu\"` and `pos` \u003d 15, so `slice` would be `\"hahahaha hihihi\"`. So the rewrite should behave the same if this assumption is true.\n\nAlternatively, Rust\u0027s facility for \"breaking when folding\" is to use `try_fold`, like:\n```\nlet (ControlFlow::Continue(start) | ControlFlow::Break(start)) \u003d\n    slice.split(\" \").try_fold(0, |acc, s| match acc + s.len() + 1 {\n        x if x \u003c\u003d pos \u003d\u003e ControlFlow::Continue(x),\n        _ \u003d\u003e ControlFlow::Break(acc),\n    });\n```\n\nIf that\u0027s more confusing, okay to leave the code as it is.",
